where is home do you have a city or county in mind? do you already have employment? wife and kids? i already have a couple much better homes and prices i could link you that ive been looking at. i have been looking at buying myself for awhile ill give you some of my best picks. it will be a few years before i have the money saved up to buy anyway. 

Edit: future employment city or if no current plans, the type of career you are thinking about going into. are the most important here.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

The hardest thing (for both of you) is to make the change from parent\child relationship to adult\adult relationship.  My mum and I are still working on it; and, we've a decade on you.

It takes not only respect, but also concerted effort from **both** parties.  

Best of luck  {{Bowchickawowsku}}

Hey, look--he asked \*you\* out. Out of all the women he could have chosen, he chose \*you\*. The hard part is over--you know he wants to go out with you. Just be yourself! You got this! Let the conversation go naturally--ask him about himself and then talk about things you have in common. As far as the sex goes--again, do NOT put pressure on yourself. You may not even go that far yet. Let things happen naturally. And don't worry about your boobs, girl--everyone who has boobies know they sag a bit. I guarantee he won't care. As the beautiful Halle Berry said, 'It's called gravity.'

&#x200B;

Okay, you got this! You got this!! Go out and the best time of your life! He \*wants\* to go out with you because he likes you--remember that and GOOD LUCK!! :)

&#x200B;

Check your credit report. 

&#x200B;

[https://www.annualcreditreport.com/index.action](https://www.annualcreditreport.com/index.action)

He was fucking with her head.

&#x200B;

People *expect you* to blow up, break their shit and throw them out. If you do that then it's way easier for them to pretend that they didn't do anything wrong. What he basically did was removed violent emotion from the situation in a way that forced her to become acutely self-aware of what she'd done to him. Chances are she's going to think about this for a long time.

&#x200B;

It's easy to forget when someone's "mean" to you. The way he subverted her expectations of what was going to happen when he found out can totally destroy someone as much as treating someone as if they never meant anything to you.
